From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:27:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 32/34] coherent: a late batch keeps held records and owes them
 the copy in of its writes

A late batch's copy back now covers every running record. Records held for
an event (a batch not planned) are kept (State::kept): they still land at
their completion, and their command buffer owes its next batch a copy in of
what other imports wrote since the late batch's first kept write
(shadow_lazy::owed_copies_in, through path 4's beside_since/taking_beside),
so the record's landing carries the write instead of covering it.

Closes the gap of lane ..._planned_in_part_elsewhere_after (reader writes,
signals, waits, then works off the surface; the writer's write was lost).
plan_left now counts kept records (exact); plan_left_planned only writes the
surface did not keep or open snapshots (gate 0); plan_owed_copies_in counts
the copies in. Demotion does not close it: it lands running records at
completion too.

Lanes: 10 late/held lanes pass; surface+event 170 passed, 1 known failure
(ycbcr_textures), as at base; runtime unit tests 73 passed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
